WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.575
DAX is the formula language of Power BI.

2
00:00:03.575 --> 00:00:07.147
On this page we compare two ways of counting.

3
00:00:07.147 --> 00:00:13.100
The first card uses COUNT, and it shows twenty two products and twenty two categories.

4
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:19.360
Now I create a new measure, called Number of Products, Remove Duplicates.

5
00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:24.720
The formula uses DISTINCTCOUNT on the Product column of the Product table.

6
00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:27.400
DISTINCTCOUNT counts each value only once.

7
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:42.850
I copy the card visual, paste it, and place the new measure in it.

8
00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:47.700
For products, the result is still twenty two, because every product name is different.

9
00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:33.100
Next, a second measure: Number of Category, Remove Duplicates, using DISTINCTCOUNT on the Category column.

10
00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:57.140
Now the difference is clear.

11
00:01:57.140 --> 00:02:03.132
COUNT gave twenty two categories, one for every row, but DISTINCTCOUNT gives three, because

12
00:02:03.132 --> 00:02:05.700
there are only three unique categories.

13
00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:12.642
In the Format pane I adjust the canvas settings, so the page has enough

14
00:02:12.642 --> 00:02:14.300
room for all the cards.

15
00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:35.600
So remember: use COUNT when you want every row, and DISTINCTCOUNT when you want

16
00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:40.400
unique values, such as the number of different sites, villages, or beneficiaries.

